userStories.description:
Install the MCP SDK and create the MCP server entry point that exposes Rorca's Express API as MCP tools. The MCP server runs as a stdio transport (Claude Code connects to it via `claude mcp add`).

Install in ~/rorca/backend/:
```bash
npm install @modelcontextprotocol/sdk
```

File: ~/rorca/backend/src/mcp/server.ts
```typescript
import { McpServer } from '@modelcontextprotocol/sdk/server/mcp.js';
import { StdioServerTransport } from '@modelcontextprotocol/sdk/server/stdio.js';
import { z } from 'zod';
import * as dotenv from 'dotenv';
import * as path from 'path';

dotenv.config({ path: path.resolve(__dirname, '../../.env') });

const RORCA_API = process.env.RORCA_API_URL || 'http://localhost:3030';

export const server = new McpServer({
  name: 'rorca',
  version: '1.0.0',
});

// Tools registered in M-002 through M-006

async function main() {
  const transport = new StdioServerTransport();
  await server.connect(transport);
}

main().catch(console.error);
```

Add to backend/package.json scripts:
```json
"mcp": "npx tsx src/mcp/server.ts"
```

Update backend/tsconfig.json to ensure `src/mcp/` is included in compilation.

File: ~/rorca/backend/src/mcp/__tests__/server.test.ts
- Test: McpServer instance has name 'rorca' and version '1.0.0'
- Test: RORCA_API falls back to 'http://localhost:3030' when env not set
- Test: server.ts exports `server` (McpServer instance)

Note: The MCP server runs alongside the Express server (not instead of it). The Express API remains the source of truth; MCP is a thin wrapper.

The headline MCP tool. Calls GET /api/direction-stack/synthesize on the Express API and returns the full synthesized Direction Stack string. This is what makes Rorca worth running — Claude Code gets the full AI context (global brain + domain profile + project brief + spec brief + story annotations) injected with a single tool call.

Add to ~/rorca/backend/src/mcp/server.ts (after the server declaration):
```typescript
server.tool(
  'rorca_get_context',
  'Get the synthesized Direction Stack for a workspace. Returns a single string containing all direction layers (L1 global brain, L2 domain profile, L3 project brief, L4 spec brief, L5 story annotations) merged in priority order. Use this to inject full AI context at the start of any spec generation or implementation session.',
  {
    workspaceId: z.string().describe('Rorca workspace ID (from rorca_list_workspaces or settings)'),
    specBrief: z.string().optional().describe('L4: one-paragraph description of the specific spec being worked on'),
    storyAnnotations: z.string().optional().describe('L5: story-level context, acceptance criteria notes, or implementation hints'),
  },
  async ({ workspaceId, specBrief, storyAnnotations }) => {
    const params = new URLSearchParams({ workspaceId });
    if (specBrief) params.set('specBrief', specBrief);
    if (storyAnnotations) params.set('storyAnnotations', storyAnnotations);
    const res = await fetch(`${RORCA_API}/api/direction-stack/synthesize?${params}`);
    if (!res.ok) throw new Error(`Direction Stack synthesis failed: ${res.status}`);
    const { context } = await res.json() as { context: string };
    return { content: [{ type: 'text', text: context }] };
  }
);
```

Note: This calls the GET /api/direction-stack/synthesize endpoint built in Phase 1. It does NOT duplicate the synthesis logic — MCP is a thin HTTP wrapper only.

