MCP tool that calls POST /api/specs/generate on the Express API. Takes a workspace ID and spec brief, returns the generated spec JSON (with userStories array). This is the primary authoring tool — Claude Code can generate specs without opening the browser UI.

Add to server.ts:
```typescript
server.tool(
  'rorca_generate_spec',
  'Generate a spec JSON (with userStories array) from a spec brief. Calls the Rorca synthesis engine which injects the full Direction Stack before sending to the LLM. Returns the generated spec as a JSON string ready to save as prd.json or submit for review.',
  {
    workspaceId: z.string().describe('Rorca workspace ID'),
    specBrief: z.string().describe('One-paragraph description of the feature or system to spec out'),
    title: z.string().describe('Short title for the spec (used as filename slug)'),
    storyCount: z.number().min(1).max(40).optional().default(8).describe('Target number of user stories (default 8)'),
    includeDiagrams: z.boolean().optional().default(true).describe('Whether to include Mermaid and ASCII diagrams in output'),
  },
  async ({ workspaceId, specBrief, title, storyCount, includeDiagrams }) => {
    const res = await fetch(`${RORCA_API}/api/specs/generate`, {
      method: 'POST',
      headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
      body: JSON.stringify({ workspaceId, specBrief, title, storyCount, includeDiagrams }),
    });
    if (!res.ok) {
      const err = await res.text();
      throw new Error(`Spec generation failed (${res.status}): ${err}`);
    }
    const spec = await res.json();
    return {
      content: [
        { type: 'text', text: `Generated spec: ${title}\n\n${JSON.stringify(spec, null, 2)}` }
      ]
    };
  }
);
```

