MCP tool to list specs in pending/ and approved/ directories. Useful for checking what's ready to run without opening the UI.

Add to server.ts:
```typescript
server.tool(
  'rorca_list_specs',
  'List all specs in a workspace. Returns specs grouped by status: pending (generated, awaiting review), approved (ready to run via Ralph Loop), and running (currently executing in a pipeline). Useful for checking queue state before starting a pipeline.',
  {
    workspaceId: z.string().describe('Rorca workspace ID'),
    status: z.enum(['pending', 'approved', 'all']).optional().default('all').describe('Filter by spec status'),
  },
  async ({ workspaceId, status }) => {
    const res = await fetch(`${RORCA_API}/api/specs?workspaceId=${workspaceId}&status=${status}`);
    if (!res.ok) throw new Error(`Failed to list specs: ${res.status}`);
    const specs = await res.json() as Array<{ id: string; title: string; status: string; storyCount: number; createdAt: string }>;
    if (specs.length === 0) {
      return { content: [{ type: 'text', text: `No specs found for workspace ${workspaceId} (filter: ${status})` }] };
    }
    const lines = specs.map(s =>
      `[${s.status.toUpperCase()}] ${s.title} (${s.storyCount} stories) — ${s.id}`
    );
    return { content: [{ type: 'text', text: lines.join('\n') }] };
  }
);
```

